Code snippets: There are [[regular code snippets]], [[code snippets that escape backticks]], and [[code snippets that contain style characters and tokens]], and [[code snippets on boundaries]].

Code snippets on boundaries: This is a `regular code snippet`, and these are backticks in tw`o word`s, which should not be stylized. (`This is a backtick starting after a parentheses`), this is *a `code snippet`* in bold text. This is a `code snippet ending after a period.`, and here is a `code snippet ending before a period`. Here is a `code snippet ending with a comma`, and this is a "`code snippet` in quotation marks," and this is "another `one`".

Regular code snippets:
This is a `code snippet`.

Code snippets that escape backticks:
This is a `code snippet that contains an escaped backtick \` but also intentional backslashes \\ eg, and also intentional double backticks eg \\\\ etc`.

Code snippets that contain style characters and tokens:
This is a `code snippet that contains _style characters_ and style tokens like {{OPEN_}} abc {{CLOSE_}}`.

